==English==

===Etymology===
1610s, from {{etyl|la|en}} ''[[pituitarius]]'' ([[mucous]]), from ''[[pituita]]'' ("[[clammy]] [[moisture]], [[phlegm]], [[mucus]], [[slime]]"), possibly from PIE root *peie- ("to be [[fat]], [[swell]]"). Taken as the name for the gland because it was believed that it channeled mucus to the nose. As a noun by 1899.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/pɪˈtjuːɪt(ə)ɹi/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Of or relating to the [[pituitary gland]].

